## 🧵 Level 1 (Basics – Thread + Runnable)

**Q1. Print numbers using 2 threads (odd/even)**
👉 Output:

```
Thread-1: 1 3 5 ...
Thread-2: 2 4 6 ...
```

```java
class OddEven {
    static int count = 1;
    static final int MAX = 10;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Object lock = new Object();

        Runnable odd = () -> {
            while (count <= MAX) {
                synchronized (lock) {
                    if (count % 2 != 0) {
                        System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + ": " + count++);
                        lock.notify();
                    } else {
                        try { lock.wait(); } catch (Exception e) {}
                    }
                }
            }
        };

        Runnable even = () -> {
            while (count <= MAX) {
                synchronized (lock) {
                    if (count % 2 == 0) {
                        System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + ": " + count++);
                        lock.notify();
                    } else {
                        try { lock.wait(); } catch (Exception e) {}
                    }
                }
            }
        };

        new Thread(odd, "Odd").start();
        new Thread(even, "Even").start();
    }
}
```

