## 🔁 Level 2 (Thread Coordination)

**Q2. Print ABCABCABC using 3 threads**

```java
class ABCPrinter {
    private int turn = 0;

    public synchronized void printA() throws Exception {
        while (true) {
            while (turn != 0) wait();
            System.out.print("A");
            turn = 1;
            notifyAll();
        }
    }

    public synchronized void printB() throws Exception {
        while (true) {
            while (turn != 1) wait();
            System.out.print("B");
            turn = 2;
            notifyAll();
        }
    }

    public synchronized void printC() throws Exception {
        while (true) {
            while (turn != 2) wait();
            System.out.print("C");
            turn = 0;
            notifyAll();
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ABCPrinter p = new ABCPrinter();
        new Thread(() -> { try { p.printA(); } catch (Exception e) {} }).start();
        new Thread(() -> { try { p.printB(); } catch (Exception e) {} }).start();
        new Thread(() -> { try { p.printC(); } catch (Exception e) {} }).start();
    }
}
```

