### **Using `@Async` for Asynchronous Processing**

#### **Enable Async Support**

Add `@EnableAsync` in the main application class or a config class.

```java
@Configuration
@EnableAsync
public class AsyncConfig {
}
```

#### **Service Layer with `@Async`**

```java
@Service
public class NotificationService {

    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(NotificationService.class);

    @Async
    public CompletableFuture<String> sendNotification(String email) {
        logger.info("Sending email to {}", email);
        try {
            Thread.sleep(3000); // Simulate delay
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture("Email sent to " + email);
    }
}
```

#### **Controller Calling Async Method**

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/notifications")
public class NotificationController {
    private final NotificationService notificationService;

    public NotificationController(NotificationService notificationService) {
        this.notificationService = notificationService;
    }

    @PostMapping("/send")
    public CompletableFuture<ResponseEntity<String>> sendNotification(@RequestParam String email) {
        return notificationService.sendNotification(email)
                .thenApply(ResponseEntity::ok);
    }
}
```

This allows the request to return immediately while the email processing continues in the background.

